    <item>
      <title>Smart Cursor</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/project/smart_cursor/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 18 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/project/smart_cursor/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Using YOLOv26 + PyQt to build system-wide target facilitation techniques. Credits: Xinqi Tang, Eva-Ly Jerome, Julien Gori.
Built on 
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;bubble-cursor&#34;&gt;Bubble cursor&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bubble Cursor is an area cursor, whose area grows until reaching the closest target. This essentially makes targets larger.
Original Bubble Cursor 
.
















&lt;figure  &gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;flex justify-center	&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;w-full&#34; &gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;Bubble Cursor demo&#34;
           src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/project/smart_cursor/bubblecursor.gif&#34;
           loading=&#34;lazy&#34; data-zoomable /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;dynaspot&#34;&gt;Dynaspot&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dynaspot is an area cursor whose area grows depending on the instantaneous speed, essentially it is a Bubble Cursor where the area is modulated by speed. The motivation behind this technique is that more precise selection requires slowing down. Original Dynaspot 

















&lt;figure  &gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;flex justify-center	&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;w-full&#34; &gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;Dynaspot demo&#34;
           src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/project/smart_cursor/dynaspot.gif&#34;
           loading=&#34;lazy&#34; data-zoomable /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;ninjacursor&#34;&gt;Ninjacursor&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NinjaCursor is a technique where one moves not a single cursor but an array of cursor. The actual cursor is selected with gaze. The idea is to first aim &amp;ldquo;with the eyes&amp;rdquo;, and perform finer movements with the mouse.


















&lt;figure  &gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;flex justify-center	&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;w-full&#34; &gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;Ninjacursors demo&#34;
           src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/project/smart_cursor/ninjacursors.gif&#34;
           loading=&#34;lazy&#34; data-zoomable /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;semantic-pointing&#34;&gt;Semantic Pointing&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Semantic Pointing is a technique which locally dissociates the mapping between (physical) mouse movements and (virtual) cursor movements. Concretely, this can make targets look sticky or on the contrary, repulsive
















&lt;figure  &gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;flex justify-center	&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;w-full&#34; &gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;Semantic Pointing demo&#34;
           src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/project/smart_cursor/semanticpointing.gif&#34;
           loading=&#34;lazy&#34; data-zoomable /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;</description>
